Rule 1 (out tensor must be floating or complex to avoid cast errors)
{v_2 : tensor} |= 6 ≤ dtype_(v_2) ∧ dtype_(v_2) ≤ 10
>>
Rule 2 (out tensor must have the same shape as input)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i)
>>
Rule 3 (complex input requires complex out)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if (9 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 10) then (9 ≤ dtype_(v_2) ∧ dtype_(v_2) ≤ 10)
>>
Rule 4 (integer or boolean input requires floating out)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if (dtype_(v_1) ≤ 5) then (6 ≤ dtype_(v_2) ∧ dtype_(v_2) ≤ 8)
>>
Rule 5 (input tensor can be any supported numeric/complex dtype)
{v_1 : tensor} |= 0 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 10
